---
// Header, full origin narrative, ContactCTA, Footer (SPEC.md — Pages & routes /about).
// Narrative rewritten in the real-content pass from xheia-content-worksheet.md — drops
// the earlier biomedical-science framing entirely (confirmed by the operator as not
// fitting: "the biomed story just doesn't fit at all") in favor of the real hook: years
// of UK contracting across varied industries. Kept deliberately service-first per that
// pass's decision — day-to-day project detail lives only in Work's case studies, not
// here. Name resolved to Hoda (first name only, no surname, by choice).
//
// Copy V2 pass: location line broadened to "across the world" (was "across the UK and
// internationally"); sector list ("life sciences, public sector, and fitness
// organisations") dropped in favor of "in the UK, across different industries" - same
// years-contracting fact, less itemized. The one concrete-proof paragraph (the
// post-acquisition six-tab dashboard result, with its /work link) is removed entirely
// per this pass's explicit instruction, replaced with a personal-motivation line -
// concrete proof now lives only on /work, not duplicated here. Hyphens, not
// em-dashes, per the sitewide sweep.
//
// Real headshot replaces the placeholder box, sized big and deliberately the only
// photographic (non-pixel-art) element on the site - a real photo reads as "stand
// out" precisely because it breaks from the site's monochrome/pixel-art visual
// language everywhere else, rather than trying to compete with it stylistically.
// astro:assets <Image> handles optimization/responsive sizing from the source file.
// Photo and "Hoda" heading sized up again ("bolder structurally" round) - a real
// masthead moment instead of a modest intro line.
//
// Name/role type in (src/scripts/typewriter.ts) once the headshot has actually
// loaded, rather than on a fixed delay - a genuine trigger instead of a guess at
// how long the image takes. Every other /approach-style section fades in via the
// same generic sitewide data-reveal mechanism; this is About's one distinct
// signature moment (Apple HIG design-improvement pass).
//
// Headshot is now a fixed-aspect-ratio crop (object-fit: cover), zoomed in enough to
// cut the hair bun off the top of the frame, per direct request - was previously the
// full uncropped source image at its native aspect ratio.
//
// Structural redesign (direct feedback that the page was "just static text, no apple
// efficiency and no pixel dna" - every other page has its own distinct signature
// interaction, About never did): the three-paragraph prose dump is replaced with a
// system-profile readout - a labeled fact table (focus/experience/stack/availability)
// in the terminal register, framed with PillarBlock's exact one-box recipe. This is
// About's answer to "distinct interaction per section" (BRANDFINAL §4): Home has the
// boot sequence, Contact has the terminal form, /approach has boot-menu/diagnostic/
// level-path - About gets a profile readout. Facts are drawn straight from
// BRANDFINAL §1 (experience, focus) and Tools.astro (stack) - nothing invented. The
// availability row reuses Footer's exact pulsing-dot device instead of the page
// having its own separate status line - one canonical "$ status" location instead of
// two saying the same thing.
//
// Round two, direct feedback: the two prose paragraphs (origin story, AI pivot) just
// restated the readout's EXPERIENCE and FOCUS rows in sentence form - literal
// duplication, not two different things. Cut both entirely rather than trying to
// reword around the overlap. The page is now three distinct beats, nothing repeated:
// masthead (who), readout (the facts), pull-quote (why it matters to me) - fewer
// words, no filler.
//
// The photo itself was "just sitting there" - static from first paint, no motion,
// the one place on the page doing nothing. It now resolves into focus on load: a
// steps()-timed blur/grayscale clear plus a top-down clip-path wipe (same
// "materializing pixel-by-pixel" idea as the sitewide [data-reveal] steps() easing,
// applied to a photo instead of a fade), with a small mono "operator.jpg" filename
// tag + loading bar underneath - the site's boot-check bar vocabulary applied to the
// one non-pixel-art element on the page. Pure CSS animation (autoplays on paint, no
// JS/class toggle) so a no-JS visitor still sees the photo resolve normally rather
// than getting stuck in a blurred, JS-dependent state - and it's disabled outright
// under prefers-reduced-motion, image visible immediately.
//
// Smoothness pass (explicit request - "drastic, no simplicity," Apple HIG's Motion
// guidance on fluid, physically-plausible feedback): the load-in choreography swaps
// steps() for a real deceleration curve (cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1), the same
// "settles into place" curve Apple's own motion relies on) across the photo resolve,
// its loading bar, and the story section's reveal - one coordinated moment instead
// of several separately-timed effects. This is deliberately different from the
// sitewide [data-reveal]/SectionLoader steps() convention used on data-heavy grids
// (Capabilities, PillarBlock, Tools) - About is the one page about a person, not a
// module list, so its motion register is warmer/fluid rather than mechanical, an
// intentional per-page distinction rather than a sitewide change. Added: a soft
// ambient glow that blooms in behind the photo as it resolves (depth/materials, HIG
// §Materials), a hover zoom on the photo (image scales inside its fixed frame,
// clipped by overflow:hidden - the frame itself never moves, so it can't disturb
// layout), a hover highlight sweep per readout row, and the pull-quote's accent bar
// now draws itself downward on reveal instead of appearing instantly. All of it
// still respects prefers-reduced-motion - full states with zero animation.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import PageIntroAtmosphere from '../components/PageIntroAtmosphere.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/hoda-headshot.png';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - Hoda"
  description="I'm Hoda - a full-stack data consultant who's spent four-plus years contracting across the UK."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content">
    <PageIntroAtmosphere>
      <div class="intro-row">
        <div class="photo-frame">
          <div class="headshot">
            <Image src={headshot} alt="Hoda" width={480} height={530} />
          </div>
          <p class="photo-caption">
            <span class="photo-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="photo-bar-fill"></span></span>
            operator.jpg
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="intro-text">
          <h1 id="about-name">Hoda</h1>
          <p class="role" id="about-role">
            I do full-stack data consulting under the name Xheia - based remotely,
            working with clients across the world.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </PageIntroAtmosphere>

    <div class="about-page">
      <div class="story" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">// profile</p>
        <dl class="readout">
          <div class="readout-row item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0s' }}>
            <dt>focus</dt>
            <dd>data quality &rarr; agentic AI</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="readout-row item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.15s' }}>
            <dt>experience</dt>
            <dd>4+ years, UK contracting</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="readout-row item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.3s' }}>
            <dt>stack</dt>
            <dd>Azure &middot; Power BI &middot; Python &middot; SQL &middot; Power Automate</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="readout-row item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.45s' }}>
            <dt>availability</dt>
            <dd>
              <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              available for new work
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <p class="pull-quote item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.65s' }}>
          What keeps me doing this: I like the actual problem-solving - messy data, no
          clear starting point, figuring it out anyway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <ContactCTA />
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { typeSequence } from '../scripts/typewriter';

  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    const img = document.querySelector('.headshot img');
    const nameEl = document.getElementById('about-name');
    const roleEl = document.getElementById('about-role');
    if (!(img instanceof HTMLImageElement) || !nameEl || !roleEl) return;

    const start = () => {
      // Capture the real, server-rendered text before clearing anything, so both
      // lines' full content is known upfront and neither flashes its stale text
      // while waiting for its own turn in the sequence.
      const items = [nameEl, roleEl].map((el) => ({ el, text: el.textContent ?? '' }));
      items.forEach(({ el }) => {
        el.textContent = '';
      });
      // Direct feedback: the cursor after the role line disappeared once typing
      // finished - it should stay and keep blinking, matching Hero's own caret,
      // which persists after its boot sequence completes rather than vanishing.
      typeSequence(items, { keepCursorOnDone: true });
    };

    if (img.complete) start();
    else img.addEventListener('load', start, { once: true });
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* PageIntroAtmosphere's own content column defaults to the sitewide
     content-max-width (72rem) - narrowed here to match this page's own
     deliberate 52rem column so the masthead's left edge lines up with
     .about-page's content below it. The glow/mark backdrop itself is
     unaffected (still full-bleed) - only the content column width changes,
     same principle as /approach's page-scoped intro-atmosphere override. */
  main :global(.intro-atmosphere-content) {
    width: min(100% - 2 * var(--space-4), 52rem);
  }

  .about-page {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4) var(--space-16);
  }

  .intro-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .photo-frame {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* Portrait 4:5 crop + a generous, soft corner radius, not the sitewide
     --radius:0 - direct feedback that a hard square read as flat rather than
     "Apple." The photo is already the site's one deliberate exception to the
     pixel-art visual language (a real photograph, not pixel art); a rounded,
     portrait-oriented frame extends that same exception rather than
     introducing a new inconsistency - every other bordered/cornered element
     on the site stays sharp-cornered. box-shadow automatically follows this
     radius, so the glow rounds with it for free. */
  .headshot {
    position: relative;
    width: 19rem;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    line-height: 0;
    /* Photo's studio backdrop is chroma-keyed out (transparent PNG) - without an
       explicit background here, the transparent edges would show PageIntroAtmosphere's
       gradient/mark bleeding through behind the photo instead of a clean card. --bg
       matches the page's own background exactly in both themes, so the photo reads as
       a flat, theme-matched card floating above the atmosphere rather than a cutout
       with a visible hole. */
    background: var(--bg);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent;
    animation: photo-glow 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
    --photo-glow: 0 0 2.5rem -0.4rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-status) 45%, transparent);
  }

  /* Direct feedback: this halo is vivid and clearly visible in dark mode (signal
     green against near-black) but barely perceptible in light mode - a colored
     box-shadow blur reads far weaker against a light surrounding, independent of
     the color-mix percentage used. Bolder mix + larger blur + no negative spread
     so it reads as a genuine, deliberate glow in light mode too. */
  :global(html[data-theme='light']) .headshot {
    --photo-glow: 0 0 3rem 0.25rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-status) 85%, transparent);
  }

  @keyframes photo-glow {
    to {
      box-shadow: var(--photo-glow);
    }
  }

  .headshot :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 95%;
    animation: photo-resolve 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
    transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .headshot:hover :global(img) {
    transform: scale(1.06);
  }

  @keyframes photo-resolve {
    from {
      filter: blur(20px) grayscale(1);
      clip-path: inset(0 0 100% 0);
    }
    to {
      filter: blur(0) grayscale(0);
      clip-path: inset(0 0 0% 0);
    }
  }

  /* 13px, not 12px - the translated typography.md minimum already applied
     everywhere else this session. */
  .photo-caption {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .photo-bar {
    display: block;
    width: 3.5rem;
    height: 0.35rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .photo-bar-fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 0;
    background: var(--accent-status);
    animation: photo-bar-fill 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
  }

  @keyframes photo-bar-fill {
    to {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .headshot {
      animation: none;
      box-shadow: none;
    }

    .headshot :global(img) {
      animation: none;
      filter: none;
      clip-path: none;
      transition: none;
    }

    .headshot:hover :global(img) {
      transform: none;
    }

    .photo-bar-fill {
      animation: none;
      width: 100%;
    }
  }

  /* Exact match to Home's headline (.headline, Hero.astro) - same font,
     weight, clamp, line-height, letter-spacing, same fix already proven on
     /approach and /work. Was font-display (Press Start 2P) at a much
     smaller/lighter size - the same pixel-font-on-real-text mismatch fixed
     everywhere else. */
  .intro-text h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 3.4vw + 1.1rem, 3.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .role {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
  }

  .about-page p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .story {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .story p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Smooth, coordinated entrance for this page only - see the top comment block.
     Higher specificity than the sitewide [data-reveal]/.item-content rules in
     global.css (steps() timing), so this overrides them without touching that
     shared file. */
  .story[data-reveal] {
    transition:
      opacity 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .story[data-reveal] .item-content {
    transform: translateY(0.9rem);
    transition:
      opacity 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .story[data-reveal].is-visible .item-content {
    transform: none;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .story[data-reveal] .item-content {
      transform: none;
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  .comment-glyph {
    margin-right: 0.4em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* --accent-primary-text, not --accent-primary: full-audit finding already
     fixed sitewide - raw --accent-primary as text is 4.22:1 against Ink in
     dark mode, below the 4.5:1 minimum. Labels this now-borderless fact
     table as one group, matching the convention every other de-boxed
     data-group on the site already has (Capabilities' "loading modules...",
     Tools' "stack manifest"). */
  /* .about-page (element+class) is higher specificity than .eyebrow alone -
     .about-page .eyebrow needed, not just .eyebrow, or the broader ".about-
     page p" text-secondary rule below wins regardless of source order. */
  .about-page .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--accent-primary-text);
  }

  /* System-profile readout - no border/tinted background, matching the
     "zero borders anywhere" standard already applied to every /approach and
     /work section; the eyebrow above now does the "this is one group" job
     the box used to. */
  .readout {
    margin: 0;
    width: min(100% - 2 * var(--space-4), 34rem);
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .readout-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    margin: 0 calc(-1 * var(--space-3));
    transition: background 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .readout-row:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-primary) 8%, transparent);
  }

  .readout-row dt {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent-primary-text);
  }

  .readout-row dd {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .status-dot {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 0.5rem;
    height: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-status);
    animation: about-status-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  /* Light mode's coral is noticeably flatter than dark mode's glowing signal green -
     a small halo gives it the same "alive" quality dark mode gets for free from the
     color itself. */
  :global(html[data-theme='light']) .status-dot {
    box-shadow: 0 0 0.5rem 0.05rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-status) 70%, transparent);
  }

  @keyframes about-status-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.4;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .status-dot {
      animation: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 28rem) {
    .readout-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-1);
    }
  }

  /* font-mono, not font-display: same fix as every other page's real-text
     titles - Home's headline is 100% IBM Plex Mono. Weight bumped to 600 for
     the same presence the pixel font carried at this size. */
  .about-page .pull-quote {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2.2vw, 1.375rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .about-page .pull-quote::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 3px;
    background: var(--accent-primary);
    transform: scaleY(0);
    transform-origin: top;
    transition: transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
    transition-delay: 0.2s;
  }

  .story[data-reveal].is-visible .pull-quote::before {
    transform: scaleY(1);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .about-page .pull-quote::before {
      transform: scaleY(1);
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .intro-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .headshot {
      width: 14rem;
    }
  }
</style>
